# Skill router

Read this entry point at the start of each work request, before opening task skills. Plain conversation needs no routing. Reuse an unchanged copy already in context; re-route when the task changes.

## Select, load, work

1. Identify the requested result, task scope, and any named skill, service, or framework. For a known or named project, consult its row in [project and agent routing](project-routing.md) to select relevant skills and a suitable agent brief. Follow explicit skill requests and mandatory prerequisites.
2. Choose the matching route below. Consult only its linked catalog when the choice needs more detail; compare neighboring alternatives by their selection criteria.
3. Load the selected skill's `SKILL.md` and required companions before doing the work. Add a companion when it covers a distinct required part of the task. Similar descriptions alone are not a reason to load several skills.
4. Follow only the selected skill's relevant branches and references. Stop discovery once the task is covered. State the chosen skills briefly, then complete the work.

Choose by task fit, not familiarity. A recommendation is a scope-based starting point, not a quality benchmark. Reconsider the route when new evidence changes the task.

## Mandatory companions

- Code changes: load `ponytail` before other task skills, after reading this router. Documentation-only changes do not require it.
- Research requests: load `deep-research` after routing; if the request also changes code, load `ponytail` first. Select the research mode proportional to the request.
- Academic writing, review, or screening: also select the appropriate academic skill in the research catalog. Send manuscript text to outside AI providers only with consent for that run.
- Named products and tool prerequisites: use their required skills, such as Supabase, Google Drive, or the appropriate Figma operation. Skill selection does not authorize publishing, messaging, delegation, or other side effects beyond the request.

## Routes

| Requested result | Start here | Choose another route or companion when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Implement or fix code | `ponytail` plus the relevant specialist in [engineering](catalog/engineering.md) | `diagnosing-bugs` for reported failures or regressions; `tdd` for requested test-first development; `write-swift` for Swift. |
| Review changes or audit a repository | [Engineering review choices](catalog/engineering.md#choose-between-overlapping-skills) | `ponytail-review` for correctness and simplicity of a change; `code-review` for Standards + Spec from a fixed base; `ponytail-audit` for the whole repository. |
| Design or improve a frontend | [Design choices](catalog/design.md#choose-between-overlapping-skills) | `frontend-design` for new visual direction; `design-taste-frontend` for researched art direction; `impeccable` for an existing interface audit or refinement; `mobile-native` for mobile browser behavior. |
| Add, investigate, or remove animation | [Motion choices](catalog/design.md#choose-between-overlapping-skills) | Select implementation, performance diagnosis, read-only recommendations, or removal according to the requested result. |
| Research, verify claims, or find literature | `deep-research` plus [research choices](catalog/research.md) as needed | `research-loop` for the full workflow: diagnose, research fixes, propose, review, delegate, run, audit, report; `research` for a primary-source Markdown deliverable; paper index for literature discovery; choose one search/extraction provider matching the requested source and available tools. |
| Write, review, or screen academic work | [Academic choices](catalog/research.md#choose-between-overlapping-skills) | `academic-paper` to write/revise; `academic-paper-reviewer` to review; `academic-pipeline` for the full research-to-finalization cycle; `sr-screener` for protocol-driven screening. |
| Analyze data, experiments, graphs, or mathematics | [Quantitative analysis choices](catalog/research.md#quantitative-analysis-additions) | Statistics and power for experiments; EDA for data quality; NetworkX for bounded graph analysis; SymPy for symbolic checks; Matplotlib or scientific-visualization for figures; `jupyter-notebook` when the deliverable is an `.ipynb`. |
| Read, create, or review a local document | [Document choices](catalog/documents.md) | The installed PDF skill covers local PDFs; use existing connected Docs/Sheets/Slides skills for those services. Local Word/Excel/PowerPoint candidates remain held for further review. |
| Edit prose to remove AI writing patterns | `unslop` in [research and writing](catalog/research.md) | Use academic guidance too when the artifact is a paper; ordinary prose edits need no academic pipeline. |
| Generate images, diagrams, or video | [Media choices](catalog/media.md) | `imagegen` for raster assets; `excalidraw-diagram-generator` for editable Excalidraw; Remotion router for videos; Figma/FigJam output uses integrations. |
| Work on databases, backend, AI apps, or Vercel | [Platform choices](catalog/platforms.md) | Choose the named database or product specialist; use the Vercel router skills for architecture and their operation-specific companions when needed. |
| Work in Figma, Google Workspace, Sites, or ChatGPT Pets | [Connected service choices](catalog/integrations.md) | Choose the actual service and operation. Use a connected tool when available and suitable; verify availability before relying on it. |
| Operate a browser | [Browser choices](catalog/integrations.md#choose-between-overlapping-skills) | Follow the current host's mandated browser first. Use `agent-browser` or `browser-use` when that execution environment is appropriate. |
| Change agent instructions, skills, or Codex setup | [Agent configuration choices](catalog/engineering.md#choose-between-overlapping-skills) | `writing-for-agents` for instruction documents; `skill-creator` for skill design; `skill-installer` for installation; `openai-docs` for Codex/OpenAI behavior and settings. |
| Use an explicitly invoked workflow | [Explicit-only catalog](catalog/explicit.md) | Includes planning, tickets, teaching, handoffs, UI prototypes, and session retrospectives. Preserve each skill's explicit-invocation boundary. |

## Availability and fallback

The catalogs inventory 180 local skill manifests on 2026-11-08, including 20 explicit-only skills and 17 project-aligned additions. The [GitHub review catalog](catalog/reviewed-library.md) records the 46 candidates, provenance, NVIDIA scan results, and held alternatives. Held candidates are not approved for automatic installation or invocation. Installed files do not guarantee tools, credentials, dependencies, or exposure in every session. Current session skill metadata and the selected `SKILL.md` are authoritative.

Resolve a selected skill from the session's current path first. Catalog links are installation snapshots; plugin cache versions can change. If a link is stale, locate that skill's current manifest instead of installing a second copy.

For a skill absent from the catalogs, search the current session's skill names/descriptions by task keywords. Read only plausible candidates. If a specialized task still has no match, search `C:/Users/ethan/.agents/skill-library/antigravity-awesome-skills/skills_index.json` and `C:/Users/ethan/.agents/skill-library/gws-cli/skills/`, then read the best-fitting manifest. If none fits, say so briefly and proceed using the available tools.

## Maintenance

When installing, removing, renaming, or changing a skill's routing description or invocation policy, update its catalog entry and any affected route here. Keep this entry point compact; put domain details in the matching catalog. Read frontmatter for inventory maintenance, rather than loading every skill body.

This router controls selection; it does not hide skill metadata that the host already supplies. Follow higher-priority host instructions when they impose additional prerequisites.

Design basis: [OpenAI guidance on skill descriptions and progressive disclosure](https://developers.openai.com/blog/rethinking-skills-and-prompts-for-gpt-6-astra).



